From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:59:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: stmpe: handle STMPE1801 read-to-clear interrupts

The STMPE1801 interrupt status register is read-only and clears when
read. Writing handled bits back is both unnecessary and contrary to its
register definition.

Retain write-one-to-clear handling for the other variants and skip the
status write for STMPE1801.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/mfd/stmpe.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c b/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c
index 3c5c2f157f..362471de3b 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/stmpe.c
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ static const struct mfd_cell stmpe_gpio_cell_noirq = {
 };
 
 /*
- * Keypad (1601, 2401, 2403)
+ * Keypad (1601, 1801, 2401, 2403)
  */
 
 static struct resource stmpe_keypad_resources[] = {
@@ -1123,7 +1123,9 @@ static irqreturn_t stmpe_irq(int irq, void *data)
 			status &= ~(1 << bit);
 		}
 
-		stmpe_reg_write(stmpe, israddr + i, clear);
+		/* STMPE1801 interrupt status is read-only and read-to-clear. */
+		if (variant->id_val != STMPE1801_ID)
+			stmpe_reg_write(stmpe, israddr + i, clear);
 	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
